WEBVTT

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.220
Hey, there he is!

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.390
Now
selling
chilled
noodles

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:11.850
Now
selling
chilled
noodles

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:08.220
You know that Iroha Igarashi
stopped coming here, right?

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.430
Well, that guy's been like a walking corpse ever since.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:11.800
Tsutsui from Class A.

00:00:11.850 --> 00:00:20.510
D
A
A
A
A
Z
E

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.430
Igarashi? She went overseas, didn't she?
To study abroad or something?

00:00:15.430 --> 00:00:16.970
I don't know.

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:20.470
But I guess this means she was just
playing him all that time.

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.300
Oh please, we all knew that from the start.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.760
Hey! Pull yourself together, stupid!

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.850
How long are you gonna mope around?

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:36.800
Huh?

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.890
Wait a minute, Tsutsui!

00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:42.140
Grrr!
Grrr!

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:45.300
All this because a girl dumped you? You're pathetic.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.470
Her parents had to move, and she had to go with them...
What was she supposed to do?

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:51.550
Never mind that, you have entrance exams.
Do you understand that?

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.600
I don't care about entrance exams...

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.260
It just... doesn't matter anymore.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:02.140
Oh, really? Well, fine then!

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.970
I never gave a damn what happened
to you to begin with.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.890
But we are trying to accomplish things right now.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.890
And it's distracting to have somebody like you
moping around right in front of us!

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.220
So get lost!

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:13.970
You're right.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.050
I'm sorry.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:15.970
Tsutsui!

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.850
Th-that was going too far, Takanashi!

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.550
This is really hard for him!

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.510
Like I care.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.260
But...

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:42.510
Tsutsui!

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.760
I brought us some snacks. You hungry?

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.550
I'll pass.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:50.930
Thanks.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:53.470
Tsutsui.

00:01:54.760 --> 00:02:00.220
We don't know anything about what happened.
Do we really have to just forget all about Igarashi?

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:05.220
We were only friends for six months.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:08.100
Is that all we were worth to her?

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:10.300
No.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:14.010
She's...

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:16.510
She's not that kind of person.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:19.680
Stop it.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.260
Don't carry it all yourself.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.300
Tsutsui.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:48.600
Konna tokoro de naitetatte

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:54.600
Daremo kizuki ya shinai wakatterunda

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:58.300
Nanmo nakatta ka no you ni

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:04.050
Kako o keshisatte sekai dake susunde yuku

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.890
Kimi o utsusu to kimeta film nanoni

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:13.390
Tamatte yuku soko nashi no sora

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:15.220
Wasuretatte kiechainai

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:18.140
Ano itami wa hora, nan dattakke?

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:23.800
Kawaru keshiki mayotte shimatta nara

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:27.930
Ano uta o omoidashite miyou ka

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:33.470
Sou ne, kanashii koto mo futari nara

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:37.260
Takaramono ni natte yuku hazu sa

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:46.430
Nijinde mo kienakatta

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:51.800
Ano hi no kimi o misetai

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:06.470
Episode 23
Regarding My Last Promise to Her.

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:05.350
I know attendance is optional,

00:04:05.350 --> 00:04:08.350
but I can't believe Tsutsui actually stopped coming.

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:11.390
Do you think he's really not going
to take any entrance exams?

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.720
Who cares? We have our own problems to deal with.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:18.550
If he's throwing his life away over a girl,
he's just a hopeless idiot.

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:23.260
Igarashi is pretty heartless, too. Up and leaving like-

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:30.260
Wh-what's wrong, Ito?

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.760
If you know something, then tell us. Now.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.930
Is that... true?

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.430
He said it seemed like it would be too painful for her
to say goodbye to all of us.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:57.140
And I bet she just couldn't bring herself
to tell us that she was sick.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.010
And Tsutsui says...

00:04:59.180 --> 00:05:02.050
He knew it would make us sad to hear about all this.

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:04.220
So he couldn't say anything.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.890
That guy is such an idiot.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:11.510
You're an idiot!

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:14.260
All those things you said to him... You were terrible!

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:18.890
You remember how Igarashi said
she didn't need friends?

00:05:19.140 --> 00:05:19.800
Yeah.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.510
But we were her friends, weren't we?

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:25.050
Yeah...

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:32.930
Thanks for having me.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:37.050
Big Brother, can Kaoru and I have some flan?

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:37.850
Sure.

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.600
Here, Kaoru!

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:40.680
Thanks.

00:05:40.890 --> 00:05:45.300
So, your brother... He stopped coming to school.
What does he do at home?

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:46.550
I dunno.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:50.470
He just kind of sits there like an empty husk.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.600
Well, you better give him a kick in the pants.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.300
At the rate he's going,
he's not gonna make it into college.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:56.720
It's not my problem.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.930
I know he's hurt because Iroha broke up with him.

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:03.050
But that's no reason to give up on everything.

00:06:04.140 --> 00:06:05.800
I have no sympathy for him.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.260
Well, I guess you would think that.

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:23.930
May I be excused?

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:25.050
What?

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.220
Hikari, you're not going to eat?

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:30.930
Honestly, I worry about that boy.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.100
It's that attitude that makes girls want to dump him.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:34.430
Um, actually.

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.010
I heard more about Big Sister Iroha.

00:06:42.390 --> 00:06:43.100
Mom?

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:45.850
My stupid, stupid boy!

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:48.300
What are you doing, acting like some tragic hero?

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:57.970
Don't you realize that you're not the one
who's hurting the most right now? Iroha is!

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:04.720
That lovely girl. Poor Iroha...

00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:09.260
Do you think she would be happy
to see you moping like this?

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:13.260
No! She would be disappointed to realize
what a useless lump she was dating!

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:15.220
Don't get depressed yet! You'll jinx it!

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:16.220
Stupid!

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:00.760
College
Testing
Center
TK
University
Test

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.850
Entrance Exam Ticket

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:41.800
Hey! Wait, please!

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.680
C-can I help you?

00:08:57.680 --> 00:08:59.640
What am I supposed to do?

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.350
Don't cry, Tsutsui!

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:16.300
The way you've been, it'd be nuts if you actually
did get into Tokyo U on the first try.

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.180
Th-that's right, Tsutsui!

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:21.010
But if I know you, you'll definitely get in next year!

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:23.930
It'll be nice to take a year off from school.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.550
Of course, I passed, though.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:28.350
But you've always lived life like a kid
who wouldn't make it into college.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:31.510
You need to learn when to stop talking, Takanashi!

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:32.430
He's right!

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:36.010
This is the one time in his life you could stand
to be nice to him, Takanashi!

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:37.300
My friends...

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.800
Don't worry.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.050
I may have passed...

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:45.180
But when I'm absolutely dying of boredom,
I might not mind hanging out with you.

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:55.600
What the-?! You did get in!

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:56.600
Let me see!

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:58.510
What? You did get in?

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:00.510
You passed the test, Tsutsui?!

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:03.140
Don't scare us like that, stupid! Way to confuse us!

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:05.260
Give me back my words of comfort!

00:10:05.260 --> 00:10:07.260
Act a little happier, Tsutsui!

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:10.140
It's just...

00:10:11.680 --> 00:10:13.760
It really didn't make any difference.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.760
My future still won't have her in it.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:17.970
It doesn't matter.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.510
I wanted to forget the whole thing.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:21.430
I did it!

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.140
Congrats!

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:22.800
But...

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.220
We'll try again next year.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:25.470
...it's no use.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.140
I couldn't do it.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.680
I can't forget any of it.

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:34.050
Well, why should you have to?

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:40.470
She's right. Stop trying to forget everything...
That's the easy way out.

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.390
You're an emo, self-loathing, stupid otaku.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:45.680
That's who you are, Tsutsui! Remember that!

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:47.640
But...

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:51.600
For some reason, you're the man Igarashi
chose to spend her last months with.

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:54.010
Don't try to forget that.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:57.600
And we won't, either. We'll always remember Igarashi.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:03.470
Besides, you don't get to go forgetting us, too.
You're too stupid for that.

00:11:06.300 --> 00:11:07.260
Tsutsun.

00:11:09.550 --> 00:11:11.100
This is goodbye.

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:14.800
Even if you do forget...

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:17.350
I never will.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:22.890
I had nothing in my life...

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:25.300
before I met you.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:30.180
You gave me everything.

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:35.640
There's no way I could ever forget you.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:43.890
That's not true at all.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:48.890
You've had so many blessings in your life, Tsutsun.

00:11:49.550 --> 00:11:53.640
And I'm sure you'll find many, many more.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:58.350
It won't be long before there's no room left for me.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:01.680
So, Tsutsun...

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:06.180
would you just promise me one thing?

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:08.890
One last promise.

00:12:09.930 --> 00:12:11.220
Promise...

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:13.720
you'll forget me.

00:12:15.760 --> 00:12:19.760
Because you are going to live on into the future.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:25.970
Well, we all got into college.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:28.350
We're moving forward.

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:30.680
It's okay to take it slow.

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:32.180
Yeah.

00:12:33.720 --> 00:12:35.390
I figured it out.

00:12:36.510 --> 00:12:39.300
I finally figured out what it is you left me.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:44.550
How are you doing these days?

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:48.300
Are you still fighting, all alone?

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:51.600
It hurts.

00:12:52.640 --> 00:12:53.800
But...

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:56.890
all we can do is move forward.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:00.800
Is it okay...

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:03.220
to move on?

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.260
I finished the proposal you asked for, sir.

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:16.640
You always work so fast, Tsutsui.

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:20.760
If you don't need anything else,
I would like to go home early.

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.140
That will be fine.

00:13:22.140 --> 00:13:25.140
I always trust you to do a good job.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:26.550
Thank you, sir.

00:13:26.930 --> 00:13:29.260
Tsutsui is so amazing.

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:31.970
I heard they're already talking about promoting him.

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:35.930
But it doesn't go to his head at all.
He's still so humble and down-to-Earth.

00:13:35.930 --> 00:13:37.760
Isn't he the best?

00:13:38.140 --> 00:13:39.930
You all done, Tsutsui?

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:40.800
Yeah.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:42.430
You wanna get some drinks tonight?

00:13:42.430 --> 00:13:45.010
I'm working on that project with Division 3,

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.680
and I wanted to ask you some things about it.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:49.800
Oh, sorry. Not today. I have plans this evening.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:51.220
Oh.

00:13:51.220 --> 00:13:52.850
Some other time.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:54.390
I'll see you later, Shinozaki.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:55.930
See you later.

00:13:57.010 --> 00:14:00.390
Sometimes, it's like Tsutsui just vanishes
at the end of the day.

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:02.220
Yeah, seems so.

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:04.850
I wonder...

00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:07.300
if he does have a girlfriend.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:16.260
DJUNGARIAN

00:14:14.350 --> 00:14:16.720
Blade of Djungarian!

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:19.800
I... I made it.

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:24.140
I'm 25 years old now.

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:28.850
After college, I went to work
at a general trading company.

00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.800
As for my friends...

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:32.850
Mechanical Design
Yuto Ito

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:37.640
Hello?

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.350
Hey, Tsutsui. Come hang out with me tonight.

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.600
You know it's a weekday.

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:44.850
Yeah, but I'm in between stuff at work.

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:46.550
Ito and Arisa will be there.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:48.510
It's a bar in Shinjuku called Beone.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:50.970
You can look up how to get there. See you.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:53.760
He's as demanding as ever.

00:14:54.050 --> 00:14:58.010
Bar Beone

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:57.800
Hey, Tsutsui! Over here!

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:00.010
You finally made it.

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:01.220
You know...

00:15:01.470 --> 00:15:03.430
You were lucky today.

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:06.970
The only reason I wasn't at work is that
I finished early so I could watch Ito's anime.

00:15:07.100 --> 00:15:09.100
I know. That's why I called.

00:15:09.390 --> 00:15:11.390
It's good to see you, Tsutsui.

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:12.510
Ito.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.510
Another good episode.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.350
I was gonna email you about it.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:18.600
Thanks for watching every week!

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.930
I record every episode, too!

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:23.430
My work makes it so I can't watch it when it airs.

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:25.850
Anyway, Tsutsui, what do you want to drink?

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:27.350
I'll have one of those.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:28.550
Excuse me!

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.300
We'd like another wine glass!

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:33.350
Oh, and I'd like a refill of my oolong tea, please!

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:37.430
Ishino? But you're usually
such a drinking fiend. What gives?

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:40.050
What do you mean, "drinking fiend"?

00:15:41.260 --> 00:15:43.930
Actually, we have an announcement.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.680
I see. Congratulations.

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.850
Come on man, let me say it!

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:54.180
What? I-Ishino, does this mean...?

00:15:54.430 --> 00:15:56.760
I'm three months pregnant now!

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:59.550
So I figure it's a good time
to change my name to Arisa Takanashi!

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:02.640
Congratulations. I wish you years of happiness.

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:03.640
What?

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:06.390
Don't you think you could be
a little more excited about this?

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:09.640
Well, with all your fighting, breaking up,
getting back together again...

00:16:09.640 --> 00:16:12.010
you've messed with our emotions way too much already.

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:14.100
The important thing is that you've settled down.

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:16.890
How will I afford this?

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:19.390
You work for a pretty good company, Takanashi.

00:16:19.390 --> 00:16:21.470
And your dream is to be an IT billionaire.

00:16:21.470 --> 00:16:24.180
Unlike you, I still have a long way to go.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:25.970
Anzu's about to start college, after all.

00:16:26.180 --> 00:16:31.100
The cost of raising a child to adulthood
plus tuition for Anzu's schooling...

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:33.550
that will be at least 34 million yen.

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.300
I see. Good luck, Breadwinner.

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:38.970
Yeah. Thanks.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:44.050
What about you? Is work treating you okay?

00:16:44.260 --> 00:16:45.640
Yeah, I guess.

00:16:45.970 --> 00:16:47.850
Do you have a girlfriend yet?

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:48.390
No.

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:51.430
Please... Don't try to tell me there are no prospects.

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:55.510
Well, there is a girl in my division
who invites me out for drinks sometimes.

00:16:55.510 --> 00:16:57.390
So you actually DO have a decent prospect!

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.180
Why don't you date her?

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:03.390
Huh? Well, it's nothing special.
We only ever talk about work.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:05.470
I don't think she's interested.

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:06.390
Huh?

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:09.100
What? You are just as dense as you ever were.

00:17:11.600 --> 00:17:13.640
Oh, that's my phone. Sorry.

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:15.470
Hello?

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:20.300
Oh, yes, if you could take that issue up
with Hayakawa in management...

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:22.100
Yes.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:24.890
Just in case, I'll make sure
to resubmit all the paperwork, too.

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:27.680
I'm sorry.

00:17:27.680 --> 00:17:29.220
Looks like I need to excuse myself.

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:30.510
Well, well.

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:32.180
You are a busy man.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:35.300
It's on me today.

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.510
In honor of the new baby.

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:40.260
Thank you, Tsutsui. I love you!

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:42.720
Hang in there, and have an adorable baby girl.

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.800
What makes you think it's a girl?

00:17:46.050 --> 00:17:47.760
See you later, Tsutsui!

00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:54.100
You know, that guy is pretty amazing.

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:58.050
He's really made something of himself.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:01.470
He's definitely not the old Tsutsui anymore.

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:06.010
We're all 25 years old now.

00:18:08.470 --> 00:18:10.800
And we're all moving forward on our own paths.

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:12.800
But...

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:14.260
I still...

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:20.930
What are you so down in the dumps about?

00:18:21.510 --> 00:18:22.800
Ezomichi!

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.100
I haven't seen you in ages!

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:30.470
You're working for a first-rate company,
and you're even managing some decent social skills!

00:18:30.470 --> 00:18:34.100
Your life is so perfect, it's like the
complete opposite of the one you had before.

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:36.720
You're right. It's more than I deserve.

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.640
Then look on the bright side!

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.470
Does it really hurt that much?

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.180
Right here.

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:47.800
No.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:51.510
I don't mind carrying this pain.

00:18:52.100 --> 00:18:56.720
I'm much happier than I ever would have been
If I'd lived my life without meeting her.

00:18:58.430 --> 00:19:00.140
Even if I never see her again...

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:03.300
Even if she's forgotten all about me...

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:05.720
Ezomichi?

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:22.260
Iroha!

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:26.850
I'll take your bag.

00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:29.260
How's it feel being back after seven years?

00:19:31.180 --> 00:19:32.970
Nothing is familiar to me.

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:39.140
This is the house we used to live in.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:41.510
Now a pair of newlyweds lives here.

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:44.220
I don't recognize it.

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:46.350
Well, there's no rush.

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:48.890
Mom and Dad decided they're coming back to Japan,

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:54.180
but you get to decide if you want to stay here or go back
to Los Angeles. They say the choice is up to you, Iroha.

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:55.800
Yeah.

00:19:56.180 --> 00:19:57.390
Next, let's...

00:19:58.220 --> 00:20:00.350
Did I walk this way a lot?

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:01.510
Yeah.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:05.180
When we were in grade school, you got stuck
in that gutter and twisted your ankle.

00:20:05.180 --> 00:20:06.680
You cried like a baby.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:09.140
I'm not sure I needed that information.

00:20:10.470 --> 00:20:12.800
And this is where you went to high school.

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:18.050
I can't remember a thing.

00:20:18.850 --> 00:20:21.970
The house, the streets... I don't know any of these places.

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:24.220
To be honest, it's scary.

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:27.220
Iroha.

00:20:28.760 --> 00:20:32.220
I told you before that we're not biologically related, right?

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:33.720
Yes.

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:36.050
But we've been together since I was five, right?

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:39.930
I admired you all that time. I love you, Iroha.

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:46.760
Personally, I don't care
if your memories ever come back.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:51.050
I will always be by your side, Iroha. Now and forever.

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:54.180
So I...

00:20:54.800 --> 00:20:58.050
I traded my memories in exchange for my life, right?

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:02.680
These last seven years, I made friends in Los Angeles,

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:06.140
and I've made a lot of really fun memories. So I'm fine.

00:21:10.350 --> 00:21:12.260
Let's go back to Los Angeles.

00:21:15.220 --> 00:21:20.680
Kareha no rhythm owari no kisetsu

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:24.760
Boku no te o hiiteta

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:36.180
Shiroi toiki wa kiekaketeita mirai (mirai)

00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:54.220
Kurikaeshi demo furidashi demo ii mujaki ni misete

00:21:55.390 --> 00:22:00.640
Aitai hito ni aeta ka na

00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:05.890
Naritai hito ni nareta ka na

00:22:06.010 --> 00:22:16.550
Kimi ga kimi rashiku iru koto de boku ga boku rashiku ireta yo

00:22:16.680 --> 00:22:21.930
Tada iki o suru kyou to iu hi ga

00:22:21.930 --> 00:22:27.180
Nani yori subarashii koto sa

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:32.510
Nanimo iranai saa ikou

00:22:32.640 --> 00:22:40.640
Shinpai nanka nanimo nai
